The JavaScript inventory includes MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD-2-Clause, PSF-2.0 and
DOMPurify's MPL-2.0 OR Apache-2.0 choice. Retain applicable upstream license and
copyright notices when distributing their code. Cargo metadata declares licenses
for every recorded dependency; platform-only packages are not all shipped on
every target. An inventory is not a completed distribution notice audit.

The app retains available Rust archive notices and exact-commit upstream
supplements (src/rust-notice-supplements.json), with standard MPL 2.0 text for
selectors and source-archive links. The resolved graph is a conservative superset
including target/build/test-only packages. Remaining notice gaps and security
findings are explicit release gates in plan.md. This is not legal clearance.
No bundled production library or font source is modified; development-only
patches are listed below. For MPL-covered components,
corresponding unmodified source is available from each version's linked registry
archive or pinned upstream repository. Keep this notice and bundled texts when
redistributing; review all vendored/system/distribution obligations for the target.

Local renderers add KaTeX (MIT code; SIL OFL 1.1 fonts as recorded in
font metadata), Mermaid (MIT), MathJax/source and TeX SVG font data (Apache-2.0),
and highlight.js (BSD-3-Clause). The generated THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt is bundled
with the app and included in standalone HTML exports. It records the installed
production graph, including packages not necessarily present in shipped chunks.
Font files remain unmodified, with their reserved names and copyright notices.

Folder matching adds ignore 0.4.33, globset, bstr and Crossbeam queue
primitives. Their MIT option and upstream notices are retained in
src/library-notices.txt and the generated bundled THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt.

Author find/replace adds @codemirror/search 6.7.1 (MIT). Its upstream
notice is retained in the generated bundled THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt.

Git uses git2 0.21.0 / libgit2 1.9.7 without SSH/HTTPS transports,
zlib and SHA-1 index checksums. Added upstream notices, including libgit2's
GPLv2 linking exception, are retained in src/git-notices.txt and the generated
bundled THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt.

The app bundles native rusqlite/SQLite support; external Pandoc, Typst and TeX
remain separately installed tools and are not distributed by Marktub.
The app uses the official tauri-plugin-single-instance 2.5.5 (MIT OR Apache-2.0),
without a general shell/network/path bridge. The app bundle includes the complete
retained Rust/JavaScript/font notice superset. Standalone HTML includes only
JavaScript/font notices relevant to its embedded assets, from
src/frontend-notices.txt, rather than unrelated Rust library texts.

